  "equipment_type": "VRF BACnet gateway (up to 16, 64 or 128 indoor units)",
  "applies_to": "Panasonic VRF (ECOi and similar) systems on one or two P-Link lines, up to 128 indoor units depending on model.",
  "summary": "An Intesis BACnet server connected to the Panasonic P-Link bus that publishes each configured outdoor and indoor unit as BACnet objects, plus 'all units' commands. The 16 and 64 unit models support BACnet IP and MS/TP; the 128 unit model is BACnet IP only. Instance numbers come from fixed formulas on line, outdoor and indoor address.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 246,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Points shown for the 'all units' commands, line 1 outdoor unit 1 and line 1 indoor unit 1 only.",
    "Outdoor unit base FO = (O x 25) + ((L - 1) x 1000) + 10000; line 1 outdoor unit 1 gives 10025.",
    "Indoor unit base FI = (U x 100) + ((L - 1) x 20000); line 1 indoor unit 1 gives 100.",
    "Room Temperature is printed as AI FI+0 in the summary tables, but its object-detail page gives AI FI+1 (the only free AI offset); FI+1 is used here, verify on site.",
    "LXOXXUXX_Bacnet ambient temperature (AO FI+3) only appears when virtual temperature is enabled in MAPS.",
    "The cover says r1.2; page headers say r1.1.",
    "The object-detail chapter also lists gateway occupancy objects (AV 0-3 setpoints, BV 0 OccupancyContinuousCheck, Unoccupancy Deadband Action with an inconsistent object type) that are not in the member tables; they are left out here."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "Intesis BACnet Server - Panasonic VRF User's Manual",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": "04/2020 r1.2",
    "url": "https://www.hms-networks.com/docs/default-source/products/intesis/manuals-and-guides---manuals/user-manual-inbacpanxxxo000.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Wire Port A to the P-Link terminals of the outdoor unit (on the 128 model Port B takes a second P-Link line), configure the units in Intesis MAPS and send the project, then map each indoor unit's _C/_S objects from its FI block. Use the 'all units' objects for global commands.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BO 100",
        "name": "LXOXXUXX_On/Off_C",
        "why": "Start/stop indoor unit"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MO 100",
        "name": "LXOXXUXX_Mode_C",
        "why": "Mode command"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AO 100",
        "name": "LXOXXUXX_Setpoint_C",
        "why": "Setpoint command"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MO 101",
        "name": "LXOXXUXX_FanSpeed_C",
        "why": "Fan speed command (1 = auto)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 100",
        "name": "LXOXXUXX_On/Off_S",
        "why": "Run status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 100",
        "name": "LXOXXUXX_Setpoint_S",
        "why": "Setpoint in use"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 101",
        "name": "LXOXXUXX_Room Temperature",
        "why": "Room (return air) temperature"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 103",
        "name": "LXOXXUXX_Communication Error IU",
        "why": "Unit offline alarm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 114",
        "name": "LXOXXUXX_Unit Error Code",
        "why": "Fault code"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "No enable point is documented; remote-controller permissions can be removed with the Allow ... from RC_C objects.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": "Enable virtual temperature for the unit in Intesis MAPS, then write the BMS room temperature to LXOXXUXX_Bacnet ambient temperature (AO FI+3). The gateway recalculates the setpoint it sends, so Setpoint_S can differ from Setpoint_C. Intesis advises using this only when the gateway is the sole source of setpoint changes.",
    "setup": [
      "Default device instance 246, configurable in MAPS.",
      "With factory settings DHCP runs for 30 s after power-up; with no DHCP answer the IP falls back to 192.168.100.246.",
      "Outdoor units are addressed 1-31 per line, indoor units 1-64 per line."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "The 128-unit model has no MS/TP.",
      "Room Temperature is printed as AI FI+0 (clashing with Setpoint_S) in the summary tables but AI FI+1 on its detail page; discover the device to confirm."
    ]
  },
